# What reaches the Docker daemon on every build.
#
# The compose services build from the repository root, so that the COPY
# directives can name paths under docker/ and deploy/. Without this file the
# root travels whole: the development SSH private key, the fixture passwords in
# .env.dev, and the full history in .git.
#
# The list is an allow list rather than a deny list. Nothing is in the context
# unless a COPY needs it, so a secret that lands in the repository tomorrow is
# out by default rather than in until somebody notices. A Dockerfile that needs
# a new path adds it here, and until it does the build says the file is not in
# the context, which is a loud failure rather than a quiet leak.
#
# The panel sources and the development keys are not here on purpose. They
# reach the containers as bind mounts at run time, which is what lets air
# rebuild on edit.

*

!deploy/
!docker/

# Inside docker/, everything except the keys. They are mounted read only at run
# time and have no business in an image layer or a build cache.
docker/keys/
